            <ArticleTitle>[Roentgen study on the topic of the &quot;aging heart&quot; with special reference to age, clinical diagnosis and therapy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>154-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Volume and linear measures of the heart (absolute as well as relative) are investigated in 640 patients (male + female). The heart size increases with increasing age. Radiological heart size shows in comparison with clinical diagnosis and findings no evidence for an old-age heart. The increasing heart size due to age is rather expression of multimorbidity during lifetime.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
